yet another new strain of the  coronavirus in the uk  this one with origins in south africa  and the health secretary announced  immediate action to stop it spreading  we've detected two cases of another new  variant of coronavirus here in the uk  both  are cases both are contacts of cases who  have traveled from south africa over the  past  few weeks first we are quarantining  cases  and close contacts of cases found here  in the uk second we're placing immediate  restrictions  on travel from south africa and finally  and most importantly  anyone in the uk who has been in south  africa  in the past fortnight and anyone who is  a close contact  of someone who's been in south africa in  the last  fortnight must quarantine  immediately the variant called 501 v2  has caused a surge of infections in  parts of south africa  it has a higher transmission rate and  may be more prevalent in the young  significantly the mutations could enable  the virus to elude  antibodies from a previous infection  that has the potential to mean  that people can get reinfected  potentially and that's something that  we're actively  studying at the moment to see how many  of the  recent infections and and the cases that  are coming through  are possibly re-infections and what  about the vaccine  we're trying to very rapidly understand  what the implications  are for for the vaccines scientists are  still getting to grips with the uk  variant  there's still no evidence that it causes  more serious disease but it has spread  nationwide with a higher proportion  found in children that could make  control more difficult if schools are  allowed to reopen in january  mostly during the lockdown period in  november  you see a statistically significant  significant  increased proportion of cases in under  15 year olds  for the bearing compared with the  nonparents you know children are  are now more like adults in their  infectiousness than they were with the  previous strains that  that will pose greater risks of of  uh in transmission involving children  mixing with each other  and you can i mean potentially there are  challenges there for  particular types of control measures and  what we want to do with schools  the chance emergence of two new variants  that evolved thousands of miles apart  underlines the importance of rolling out  the vaccine worldwide  the pandemic isn't over until it's over  everywhere  or the virus could come back to haunt us  thomas more sky news
 

